    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Mushroom 1: Lion's Mane -->
  <section class="mush-section">
    <div class="mush-inner">
      <div class="mush-badge" style="background:#EEF2FF;color:#3730A3;">THE SHAGGY ONE</div>
      <div class="mush-layout">
        <div class="mush-icon-wrap" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#EEF2FF,#C7D2FE);">
          <div class="mush-emoji">
            <img src="{{ 'lions-mane.png' | asset_url }}" alt="Lion's Mane mushroom" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mush-content">
          <h2>Lion's Mane</h2>
          <div class="mush-dose">900 mg per can · Hericium erinaceus · Fruiting body extract</div>
          <p class="mush-desc">Lion's Mane (<em>Hericium erinaceus</em>) is a shaggy white culinary mushroom, named for the cascading spines that make it look like a lion's mane, and part of traditional practices in East Asia for centuries.</p>
          <div class="mush-benefits">
            <div class="mush-benefit">
              <span class="mush-benefit-icon">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#3730A3" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 3h6l1 4H8L9 3z"/><path d="M8 7v10a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h6a1 1 0 0 0 1-1V7"/><path d="M12 11v3M11 13h2"/></svg>
              </span>
              <div><strong>What It Looks Like</strong><p>Soft, white, icicle-like spines that hang in a shaggy clump. It grows on hardwood trees, and cooks often compare its texture to crab or lobster.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="mush-benefit">
              <span class="mush-benefit-icon">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#3730A3" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M12 2v3M12 19v3M4.22 4.22l2.12 2.12M17.66 17.66l2.12 2.12M2 12h3M19 12h3M4.22 19.78l2.12-2.12M17.66 6.34l2.12-2.12"/></svg>
              </span>
              <div><strong>A Long Culinary History</strong><p>Long enjoyed as a food mushroom in China and Japan, where it goes by names like <em>hou tou gu</em> (monkey head mushroom) and <em>yamabushitake</em>.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="mush-benefit">
              <span class="mush-benefit-icon">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#3730A3" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2L4 6v6c0 5.55 3.84 10.74 8 12 4.16-1.26 8-6.45 8-12V6l-8-4z"/></svg>
              </span>
              <div><strong>900 mg in Every Can</strong><p>As fruiting body extract, in a caffeine-free sparkling drink.</p></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="mush-fact">
            <strong>The real mushroom, not a sprinkle.</strong> We use 100% fruiting body extract, the mushroom itself rather than mycelium grown on grain.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mush-divider"></div>

  <!-- Mushroom 2: Cordyceps -->
  <section class="mush-section" style="background:#FAFAFA;">
    <div class="mush-inner">
      <div class="mush-badge" style="background:#FFF7ED;color:#C2410C;">THE ORANGE ONE</div>
      <div class="mush-layout">
        <div class="mush-icon-wrap" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#FFF7ED,#FED7AA);">
          <div class="mush-emoji">
            <img src="{{ 'cordyceps.png' | asset_url }}" alt="Cordyceps militaris mushroom" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mush-content">
          <h2>Cordyceps</h2>
          <div class="mush-dose">700 mg per can · Cordyceps militaris · Fruiting body extract</div>
          <p class="mush-desc">Cordyceps (<em>Cordyceps militaris</em>) is a bright orange, club-shaped mushroom from a family with a long history in traditional Tibetan and Chinese practices. No caffeine, and not a stimulant.</p>
          <div class="mush-benefits">
            <div class="mush-benefit">
              <span class="mush-benefit-icon">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#C2410C" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3C8 4 5 8 5 12s3 8 7 9c4-1 7-5 7-9s-3-8-7-9z"/><path d="M12 8v4l2 2"/></svg>
              </span>
              <div><strong>What It Looks Like</strong><p>Slender, finger-like orange stalks that stand straight up, a little like a tiny patch of coral.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="mush-benefit">
              <span class="mush-benefit-icon">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#C2410C" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M13 2L4.5 13.5H11L10 22l9.5-11.5H13L13 2z"/></svg>
              </span>
              <div><strong>A Mountain Legend</strong><p>Stories of cordyceps go back centuries on the Tibetan plateau, where its wild cousin was found growing at high altitude.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="mush-benefit">
              <span class="mush-benefit-icon">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#C2410C" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18 8h1a4 4 0 0 1 0 8h-1"/><path d="M2 8h16v9a4 4 0 0 1-4 4H6a4 4 0 0 1-4-4V8z"/><line x1="6" y1="1" x2="6" y2="4"/><line x1="10" y1="1" x2="10" y2="4"/><line x1="14" y1="1" x2="14" y2="4"/></svg>
              </span>
              <div><strong>700 mg in Every Can</strong><p>As fruiting body extract. No caffeine and no stimulants, so the can fits any time of day.</p></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="mush-fact">
            <strong>Militaris, not sinensis.</strong> We use <em>Cordyceps militaris</em>, a species that can be cultivated. <em>C. sinensis</em> (the parasitic caterpillar fungus) is rare, expensive, and inconsistent.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mush-divider"></div>

  <!-- Mushroom 3: Reishi -->
  <section class="mush-section">
    <div class="mush-inner">
      <div class="mush-badge" style="background:#F0FDF4;color:#166534;">THE GLOSSY ONE</div>
      <div class="mush-layout">
        <div class="mush-icon-wrap" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#F0FDF4,#BBF7D0);">
          <div class="mush-emoji">
            <img src="{{ 'reishi.png' | asset_url }}" alt="Reishi (Ganoderma lucidum) mushroom" loading="lazy">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mush-content">
          <h2>Reishi</h2>
          <div class="mush-dose">400 mg per can · Ganoderma lucidum · Fruiting body extract</div>
          <p class="mush-desc">Reishi (<em>Ganoderma lucidum</em>) is a glossy, red-brown, woody mushroom that has been revered for centuries in traditional East Asian practices, where it's often called <em>lingzhi</em>.</p>
          <div class="mush-benefits">
            <div class="mush-benefit">
              <span class="mush-benefit-icon">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#166534" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 22V12"/><path d="M12 12C12 12 7 10 6 6c3 0 6 2 6 6z"/><path d="M12 12c0 0 5-2 6-6-3 0-6 2-6 6z"/></svg>
              </span>
              <div><strong>What It Looks Like</strong><p>A shiny, kidney-shaped cap that looks almost lacquered. It's tough and woody, so it's never eaten whole; traditionally it's sliced and simmered.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="mush-benefit">
              <span class="mush-benefit-icon">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#166534" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 12.79A9 9 0 1 1 11.21 3 7 7 0 0 0 21 12.79z"/></svg>
              </span>
              <div><strong>Centuries of Tradition</strong><p>Reishi shows up in Chinese art and traditional texts going back centuries, often as a symbol of good fortune.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="mush-benefit">
              <span class="mush-benefit-icon">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#166534" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2L4 6v6c0 5.55 3.84 10.74 8 12 4.16-1.26 8-6.45 8-12V6l-8-4z"/><path d="M8.5 12l2.5 2.5 4.5-4.5"/></svg>
              </span>
              <div><strong>400 mg in Every Can</strong><p>As fruiting body extract, alongside the Lion's Mane and Cordyceps.</p></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="mush-fact">
            <strong>Three mushrooms, one can.</strong> 900 mg Lion's Mane, 700 mg Cordyceps and 400 mg Reishi, all fruiting body extracts, in Blue Razzberry, Mango Mimosa and Watermelon.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

